1
00:04:55,555 --> 00:05:01,555
Death comes for all men.

2
00:09:51,111 --> 00:09:57,111
Bone Tomahawk is a western, horror, drama film directed by S. Craig Zahler.

3
00:14:46,666 --> 00:14:52,666
During a shootout in a saloon, Sheriff Hunt injures a suspicious stranger.

4
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:48,222
The doctor's assistant, wife of the local foreman, tends to him in prison.

5
00:24:37,777 --> 00:24:43,777
That night, the town is attacked and they both
disappear—only the arrow of a cannibal tribe is found.

6
00:29:33,333 --> 00:29:39,333
Hunt and a few of his men go in search of the prisoner and the foreman's wife.

7
00:34:28,888 --> 00:34:34,888
Sheriff Franklin Hunt, played by Kurt Russell.

8
00:39:24,444 --> 00:39:30,444
Arthur O'Dwyer, played by Patrick Wilson.

9
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:26,000
Chicory, played by Richard Jenkins.

10
00:49:15,555 --> 00:49:21,555
John Brooder, played by Matthew Fox.

11
00:54:11,111 --> 00:54:17,111
Samantha O'Dwyer, played by Lili Simmons.

12
00:59:06,666 --> 00:59:12,666
Purvis, played by David Arquette.

13
01:04:02,222 --> 01:04:08,222
Bone Tomahawk is a 2015 American Western film written and directed by S.

14
01:08:57,777 --> 01:09:03,777
Craig Zahler in his directorial debut, and starring Kurt Russell, Patrick Wilson, Matthew Fox, Richard
Jenkins, Lili Simmons, Evan Jonigkeit, David Arquette, Zahn McClarnon and Sid Haig.

15
01:13:53,333 --> 01:13:59,333
It was produced by Jack Heller and Dallas Sonnier.

16
01:18:48,888 --> 01:18:54,888
The film is about a small-town sheriff who leads a posse into a desolate region to rescue
three people who were abducted by a cannibalistic clan of troglodytes.

17
01:23:44,444 --> 01:23:50,444
Development of the film started when Zahler's friend and manager Sonnier recommended
creating a film adaptation of Zahler's Western novel Wraiths of the Broken Land.

18
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
Realizing that such a project could not be adapted on a low
budget, Zahler opted to write a rescue Western instead.

19
01:33:35,555 --> 01:33:41,555
Casting began in October 2014, with Peter Sarsgaard, Timothy Olyphant, and Jennifer Carpenter signed on to
play before being replaced by Wilson, Fox, and Simmons respectively due to scheduling conflicts.

20
01:38:31,111 --> 01:38:37,111
Principal photography took place in California over a
course of 21 days in October 2014.

21
01:43:26,666 --> 01:43:32,666
The premiere of Bone Tomahawk took place at Fantastic Fest on October 1, 2015.

22
01:48:22,222 --> 01:48:28,222
RLJ Entertainment gave the film a limited release on October 23, grossing over $480,000 in
theater sales and $4.32 million in home media sales against a $1.8 million budget.

23
01:53:17,777 --> 01:53:23,777
The film received mainly positive reviews, with praise for Zahler's
screenplay and direction and the performances of the ensemble cast.

24
01:58:13,333 --> 01:58:19,333
It has now become a modern cult classic.

25
02:03:08,888 --> 02:03:14,888
The film explores themes of rescue, sheriff, prisoner, ambush, poison.

26
02:08:04,444 --> 02:08:10,444
The tone is dark and emotional.
